**Impact:** At 48 bytes (1 `long` + 5 `double`), the struct exceeds the recommended ≤16-byte guideline for value types. Every arithmetic operator (`+`, `-`, `*`, `/`) constructs a new `DataSize`, eagerly computing all 6 unit values, then copies 48 bytes on return. With thousands of concurrent transfers computing throughput, this means millions of unnecessary divisions and excessive copy traffic.
**Files:** DataSize.cs:L42-50 (constructor), L53-68 (properties), L124-127 (operators)
**Fix:** Store only `Bits` (8 bytes). Compute `Bytes`, `Kilobytes`, etc. as on-demand `get`-only properties via division. This shrinks the struct to 8 bytes and eliminates 5 unused divisions per construction.

